## The overall assembly process:

### Set up

```
mkdir SEQPAIRED; cd SEQPAIRED

```

```nano SRA_SRR.txt```

```
DRS075098
DRR146814
ERS2867139
ERR2863830
```

```nano download.sh```

```
i=0
line2="hello"
while read line; do
        i=$(( i+1 ))
        if (($i % 2)) ; then
                echo $i
                mkdir $line
                line2=$line
                echo $line2
        else
            	for srr in $line
                do
                  	echo $srr
                        /usr/local/sratoolkit/prefetch $srr
                        mv /home/yuying/ncbi/public/sra/* $line2
                done
        fi
done < SRA_SRR.txt
```
```nohup bash download.sh &```

Sometimes there can be problems downloading if you are getting a lot of files so you may have to redownload some strains. Check which files are empty and redownload them
```find . -type d -empty -print```

Now convert the sra files into fastq. Make an SRA.txt file that lists the accession numbers of the strains that are in sra format. Then make a script called fastqextract.sh with ```fastqextract.sh``` and input in:
```
run=()
while read line; do
        run=$(find $line -type f)
        for id in $run
        do
          	/usr/local/sratoolkit/fastq-dump --skip-technical --outdir $line --split-files $id
        done
done < SRA.txt
```





